  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the clear best at 0.619 acc, showing that multi-profile + avgpool aggregation and multimodal fusion are both critical. The only untested dimension within this exact configuration is the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted). Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation when combining RNA and image features under the otherwise-identical best setup? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable A/B test against the current best (config_018), directly exploiting the strongest evidence while testing whether the fusion mechanism is a meaningful lever. If weighted fusion improves, it opens a new optimization axis; if not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can redirect budget toward image encoder (ViT-L) or RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt) variants with confidence that fusion is not the bottleneck."
}

